What I built (all from `apps/design/tokens.json`, no hand-copying):

- **Deterministic generator** ΓÇö `apps/windows/TeslaSync.TokenGen` (net10.0 console, added to the solution). Reads `tokens.json` ΓåÆ emits `apps/design/generated/windows/Tokens.xaml`. Has a `--check` mode that fails on drift (verified in sync).
- **Generated `Tokens.xaml`** ΓÇö Fluent/WinUI `ResourceDictionary` covering every category: typography (sizes/line-heights/letter-spacing/weights + font families), spacing scale, corner radii, motion durations/easings, elevation z + material map, the 14-color brand chart palette, and 3 `ThemeDictionaries` (Default=Dark, Light, HighContrast) with per-theme `Color`+`SolidColorBrush` for surfaces/text/accent/border/status plus `AcrylicBrush` materials. Deterministic names (`TsColorAccentBrush`, `TsChart01Brush`, `TsTypeBodyFontSize`, ΓÇª).
- **App theme dictionaries** ΓÇö `Themes/{Dark,Light,HighContrast}.xaml` map glass tokens ΓåÆ Fluent materials: **Mica** for the app root (wired via `MainWindow.SystemBackdrop = MicaBackdrop`), **Acrylic** for raised/overlay surfaces, **ThemeShadow** for depth. HighContrast defers to OS `SystemColor*` brushes (no forced brand colors, no Acrylic/Mica).
- **Wiring** ΓÇö `App.xaml` merges the tokens and the `ThemeDictionaries`; the generated file is linked as an `ms-appx:///Themes/Tokens.xaml` Page.
